---
import BlogGrid from '../components/BlogGrid.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageTitle = 'WakePerfect | Sleep Cycle Tools';
const pageDescription =
    'Use our free Sleep Time Calculator to find the best times to go to bed or wake up based on 90-minute sleep cycles. Improve your sleep quality and wake up refreshed.';
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
    <div class="container box-container">
        <h1>Sleep Time Calculator 💤</h1>
        <p class="description">
            Improve your sleep quality by waking up at the right time. Our Sleep
            Time Calculator helps you figure out the best times to go to bed or
            wake up based on natural 90-minute sleep cycles. Simply input your
            desired sleep or wake time, and we’ll handle the rest!
        </p>
        <a class="button-link" href="/sleep-time-calculator/"
            >Launch Calculator</a
        >
        <p class="note">
            The average sleep cycle lasts around 90 minutes. Aligning your
            wake-up time with the end of a cycle can help you feel more
            refreshed and alert.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="container seo-content">
        <h2>What Is a Sleep Cycle?</h2>
        <p>
            A sleep cycle typically lasts about 90 minutes and includes
            different stages of sleep—light sleep, deep sleep, and REM (rapid
            eye movement). Waking up during the lighter stages of sleep can help
            you feel more refreshed and energized compared to waking up during
            deep sleep.
        </p>

        <h2>Why Timing Matters</h2>
        <p>
            Waking up at the end of a sleep cycle helps reduce grogginess and
            sleep inertia. By using a sleep calculator, you can plan your
            bedtime or wake-up time to align with your natural sleep rhythm,
            improving your overall alertness and well-being.
        </p>

        <h2>How Much Sleep Do You Need?</h2>
        <p>
            Most adults need between 7–9 hours of sleep per night. That equates
            to about 5–6 full sleep cycles. Your individual needs may vary based
            on age, health, and lifestyle, but getting the right amount of sleep
            is critical for both physical and mental health.
        </p>

        <h2>Tips for Better Sleep</h2>
        <p>
            To improve your sleep quality, consider going to bed at the same
            time each night, avoiding screens before bed, keeping your room cool
            and dark, and avoiding caffeine late in the day. Consistency is key
            to helping your body maintain a healthy sleep routine.
        </p>

        <h2>Use Our Sleep Time Calculator</h2>
        <p>
            Whether you're planning when to go to bed or when to wake up, our
            calculator can help you find the best time based on your desired
            schedule. It's a simple but powerful tool to help you take control
            of your sleep.
        </p>

        <div class="btn-wrapper">
            <a class="button-link" href="/sleep-time-calculator/"
                >Launch Calculator</a
            >
        </div>
    </div>

    <BlogGrid />
</BaseLayout>
